   (`totem_presets.login_code`), single-use, TTL **10 min**
-  (`login_code_expires_at`), consumed atomically on success. Failed attempts
-  rate-limited per code + per IP.
-- JWT: short TTL (`expires_in: 3600`, 1h placeholder pending [open question](#open-questions))
-  with rotation/refresh defined at implementation;
-  claims carry `totem_id` + `entity_id` + `preset_id` + queue scope. Every later endpoint
-  re-validates totem `is_active` + preset `is_active` + entity subscription server-side.
-- Discord ≠ log sink: audit pairing success/failure via app logs per
-  [`../ops/logging.md`](../ops/logging.md); alert on abuse spikes only.
+  (`login_code_expires_at`), consumed atomically on success inside a
+  transaction with the preset row locked (`lockForUpdate`). Failed attempts
+  share the `totem-auth` throttle bucket (10/min per IP); when exceeded the
+  API answers `429 {"code":"rate_limited"}` (throttle exceptions on `api/*`
+  render as that JSON).
+- JWT: HS256 (`App\Support\TotemJwt`), claims `totem_id` + `entity_id` +
+  `preset_id` + `queues` (queue ids at pairing time) + `iat` + `exp` +
+  `jti`. Secret and TTL come from config `services.totem.jwt_secret` /
+  `services.totem.jwt_ttl` (env `TOTEM_JWT_SECRET` / `TOTEM_JWT_TTL`,
+  default TTL 3600; see [Configuration](#configuration)). Every later
+  endpoint re-validates totem `is_active` + preset `is_active` + entity
+  match server-side.
+- Audit, never the full code: pairing success logs
+  `totem.pairing.success` (`preset_id`, `entity_id`, `totem_id`); any
+  failure logs `totem.pairing.failed` (`reason` only:
+  `invalid_code_format` / `invalid_pairing_code`); code generation logs
+  `totem.pairing-code.generated` (`preset_id`, `entity_id`). All on the
+  `audit` channel per [`../ops/logging.md`](../ops/logging.md); alert on
+  abuse spikes only.
+
+## Authenticated endpoints
+
+`Authorization: Bearer <jwt>` on every call. `App\Http\Middleware\TotemAuth`
+(alias `totem.auth`) rejects with `401 {"code":"invalid_token"}` when the
+token is missing/invalid/expired, the totem is not found or
+`is_active = false`, the preset is not found or inactive, or the entity
+ids of claims, totem and preset disagree. On success it quietly refreshes
+`totems.last_seen_at` (failures to persist never fail the request) and
+binds `totem`, `totem_preset`, `totem_entity` and `totem_scope` to the
+request.
+
+The effective queue scope is the **intersection** of the JWT `queues` claim
+with the preset's **current** queue join, so removing a queue from the
+preset takes effect immediately for existing tokens.
+
+For all three endpoints, `{entity}` is the entity slug and must equal the
+token's entity, else `403 {"code":"forbidden"}`. `{queue}` is a queue slug
+resolved **within that entity** only: not found (including another entity's
+slug) → `404 {"code":"queue_not_found"}`; found but outside the effective
+scope → `403 {"code":"forbidden"}`.
+
+Error summary:
+
+| Status | `code` | When |
+| ------ | ------ | ---- |
+| 401 | `invalid_token` | Middleware rejection (see above) |
+| 403 | `forbidden` | Entity slug mismatch, or queue outside effective scope |
+| 404 | `queue_not_found` | Queue slug unknown within the token's entity |
+| 422 | `inactive_queue` | Queue in scope but `is_active = false` (priorities + issuance) |
+| 422 | `invalid_priority` | Priority not one of the backend-owned values (issuance) |
+| 429 | `rate_limited` | Issuance throttle (30/min, `totem-ticket` limiter) |
 
