+## CORS
+
+The totem's web build runs on a local static server. `config/cors.php`
+answers CORS on `api/*` for origins `http(s)://localhost[:port]` and
+`http(s)://127.0.0.1[:port]`, plus an optional `TOTEM_WEB_ORIGIN` env
+(exact origin string). Any other origin gets **no**
+`Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. A preflight
+`OPTIONS /api/totem/auth` from `http://localhost:8081` gets `204` with
+`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:8081`. No credentials
+(`supports_credentials: false`).
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Env | Default | Notes |
+| --- | --- | ------- | ----- |
+| `services.totem.jwt_secret` | `TOTEM_JWT_SECRET` | — | HS256 secret, ≥ 32 chars in production |
+| `services.totem.jwt_ttl` | `TOTEM_JWT_TTL` | `3600` | Seconds; returned as `expires_in` |
+| `services.totem.web_origin` | `TOTEM_WEB_ORIGIN` | — | Optional extra allowed CORS origin |
+
+`phpunit.xml` pins a ≥ 32-char test secret and TTL 3600 so the suite runs
+without a local `.env` secret.
